namespace Pscf {
namespace Rp {

/*! 
\page rp_CubicLengthDerivative_page CubicLengthDerivative

This analyzer calculates the derivative of free energy with respect to 
the unit cell size of a cubic unit cell. 

\see CubicLengthDerivative (class API)

\section rp_CubicLengthDerivative_algorithm_sec Mathematical Formula

Consider a system containing in a periodic cubic simulation cell of 
volume \f$ V = L^3 \f$, where \f$ L \f$ is the cubic cell length.
Let \f$ F \f$ denote the total free energy of the system contained
in one such a cell, in thermal energy units for which \f$ kT = 1 \f$. 
The CubicLengthDerivative analyzer computes the derivative 
\f[
    F' = \frac{\partial F}{\partial L} \quad,
\f]
where the derivative is evaluated at constant monomer volume (or 
total monomer concentration), constant volume fraction for each 
species, and constant values of all other input parameters.  

Let \f$ f_{\rm id}' \f$ denote the SCFT prediction for the 
derivative of the non-dimensional free energy per monomer, 
normalized by \f$ kT \f$, as returned by the Rp::Mixture::stress 
function for parameter index 0 of a cubic unit cell.  This quantity 
is given mathematically by 
\f[
    f_{\rm id}' 
    = -\sum_{\alpha} \frac{\phi_{\alpha}}{N_{\alpha}}
       \frac{\partial \ln Q_{\alpha}}{\partial L}
\f]
Here, 
\f$ \alpha \f$ is an index for polymeric species, and 
\f$ \phi_{\alpha} \f$, \f$ N_{\alpha} \f$, and \f$Q_{\alpha}\f$ are 
the volume fraction, total number of monomers and normalized single 
chain partitition for species \f$ \alpha \f$, respectively. This sum 
over species in this expression includes all polymeric species, but
exclude any point-particle solvent species.

The derivative \f$ F' \f$ is computed as a sum
\f[
  F' = \frac{V}{v}f_{\rm id}' + \frac{3V}{L} H_{\rm f}
     +  \frac{3G}{2L}
\f]
where\f$ v \f$ is monomer volume,
\f$ G \f$ is the number of grid points in the computational mesh, 
and \f$ H_{\rm f} \f$ is the value of the quadratic field contribution 
to the \ref psfts_theory_page "field theoretic Hamiltonian", as returned
by the function Simulator::fieldHamiltonian(). In systems with two 
monomer types, \f$ H_{\rm f} \f$ is given by an integral
\f[
  H_{\rm f} =
  \int \! d{\bf r} \; \left \{
  \frac{W_{-}^{2}({\bf r}) }{v \chi}
  - W_{+}^{*}({\bf r}) c_{0}
  + \frac{\chi}{4v} \right \}
\f]
where \f$ W_{+}^{*}({\bf r}) \f$ denotes a saddle-point configuration
of the pressure field and \f$ c_{0} = 1/v \f$. 

\section rp_CubicLengthDerivative_parameter_sec Parameter File

The full parameter file format, including all optional parameters, is 
shown below:
\code
CubicLengthDerivative{
  interval           int
  outputFileName     string
  hasAverage*        bool    (default true)
  nSamplePerOutput*  int     (default 1)
}
\endcode
Meanings of the parameters are described briefly below:
<table>
  <tr>
    <td> <b> Label </b>  </td>
    <td> <b> Description </b>  </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td> interval </td>
    <td> number of steps between data samples </td>
  </tr>
    <tr>
     <td> outputFileName </td>
     <td> name of output file </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
     <td>hasAverage</td>
     <td>Should the average value and error analysis be output? </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
     <td>nSamplePerOutput</td>
     <td>Number of sampled values per block average, and per output</td>
  </tr>
</table>

\section rp_CubicLengthDerivative_output_sec Output
Values of the derivative \f$  F'  \f$ are computed every "interval" 
simulation steps. 

By default, block averages of nSamplerPerOutput sequential computed
values are output every interval * nSamplerPerOutput time steps. Output 
of block averages may be suppressed by setting nSamplerPerOutput to
zero.

If hasAverage is true, then at the end of the simulation:
  - average info and error analysis are output to {outputFileName}.ave
  - error analysis info are output to {outputFileName}.aer

*/

}
}
